+# Plan: JSON Patch
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md) — RFC 6902 §3–§5, RFC 6901.
+
+## Approach
+- `src/pointer.ts`: factor out and export `parsePointer(pointer): string[]` (internal, not from index); `resolvePointer` uses it.
+- `src/patch.ts`: `PatchError`, `applyPatch`. Deep-clone the document up front (own clone preserving own `__proto__` keys), mutate the clone, so failures leave inputs untouched. Values from the patch are cloned on insertion. `test` uses a structural deep-equal.
+- Export `applyPatch`, `PatchError` from `src/index.ts`. Tests in `test/patch.test.js` (against `dist`). README updated.
+
+## Constitution Check
+- I: RFC 6902 sections named; rules (atomicity, move prefix rule, `-`, test equality) implemented exactly. Root `remove` choice documented.
+- II: no dependencies. III: tests first, seen failing. IV: no mutation, atomic, `Object.defineProperty` for member writes, own-property checks, typed errors. V: strict TS, doc comments, exported. VI: two small files.
